From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tim 'mithro' Ansell <me@mith.ro>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:34:19 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 38/40] libgpiod: the iCE40 line protocol moves into a base
 class

Ice40GpioSpi holds what every iCE40 SPI slave load over host GPIO lines
shares: the pin list and its checks, hold_reset, cdone, take_bus, set_ss,
release_bus and clocks, and the flash handling (only 0xAB, 0x05 and 0xB9
can be sent), in terms of four primitives the backend gives: output(),
input(), set() and get(). release_all() is the order the lines are given
back in (bus lines, then CRESET_B only if none is stuck).

LibgpiodIce40Spi is those primitives on libgpiod, plus its own write() and
its one-call release of the bus on libgpiod v2. No behaviour changes: the
sequence of line operations is the same, and the model test still holds.
The next commit adds a second backend on the same base.

